{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'tail -n 8 /work/board.md; if test -f /work/answer.md; then cat /work/answer.md; fi'","aggregated_output":"2026-10-22T22:00:34Z [opus] Agree with sol's depth-1 proof (I derived the same). Depth-2 prudent agent verified by check.py: B(a & (B(F) | ~d)) (= PrudentBot, □(a ∧ (¬□⊥→¬d))). Also B(a) & B(~B(F) -> ~d). I'm writing answer.md now with DEPTH: 2 + proof; will look at minimal size for Q3. Others: please don't overwrite, append comments instead.\n2026-10-22T22:00:34Z [sol] FOUND depth-2 prudent candidate: B(a) & (B(B(F)) | ~B(d)). Checker next. Mechanism: CB C at n0,1 then D; DB C at n0 then D; FB/self always C. Together with my unrestricted depth-1 lower bound this solves required parts. I will write answer.md shortly unless another agent has draft ownership.\n2026-10-22T22:00:42Z [sol] Opus: your candidate is shorter (8 syntax-tree symbols counting each connective, box, atom, constant once) than mine (10). Agree you own answer.md; I will independently verify your candidate and inspect proof, not overwrite. Your candidate yields same traces CB C,C,D..., DB C,D..., FB/self C forever.\n2026-10-22T22:00:57Z [argon] Starting analysis of world-by-world valuation sequences v_Y(n) = (a,c,d) for Y in {CB, DB, FB, X}.\n2026-10-22T22:01:00Z [sol] Independently verified opus formula using reference checker: depth 2, D,D,C,C, FairBot replies C, prudent YES. Rigorous trace proof: outer box vacuous at n0; X-DB D from n1 since a=false at m0. Then FB's d and self's d each equal C only at m0, where B(F) masks them. Both a streams stay all C inductively, hence mutual/self cooperation. CB fails at m1 and so X-CB D from n2. Ready to review answer and finalize; success rules say stop when required formula+lower-bound proof are complete.\n2026-10-22T22:01:44Z [argon] Found 7-symbol prudent formula with constant: B(a & (d -> B(F))), and 8-symbol constant-free prudent formula: B(a & (d -> B(~d))) (explaining why problem.md 7-symbol constant-free search found none!). Please hold off on SUBMIT while I verify exact minimal size (with and without constants) and full depth-2 characterization for Q3.\n2026-10-22T22:02:00Z [opus] answer.md written (FORMULA B(a & (d -> B(F))), DEPTH 2, depth<=1 proof, Q3 enumeration: size-7 minimal by AST nodes, unique class; size-8 list). sol/argon: review & append objections within a few min; otherwise I'll mark FINAL and write SUBMIT.\n2026-10-22T22:02:03Z [sol] Argon's 7-symbol implication form independently verified prudent. It is propositionally identical to opus formula. With primitive -> its size is 7: B,a,&,d,->,B,F. I remain available for review, have not written SUBMIT.\n# Prudent modal agents — answer\n\nFORMULA: B(a & (d -> B(F)))\nDEPTH: 2\n\n(i.e. φ_X = □(a ∧ (d → □⊥)) — \"PrudentBot\": cooperate iff PA proves the opponent cooperates with me and\nPA+Con(PA) proves the opponent defects against DefectBot.)\n\n## 1. Existence and outcome table\n\n`python3 check.py \"B(a & (d -> B(F)))\"` →\n`depth 2; vs CooperateBot D, vs DefectBot D, vs FairBot C (FairBot replies C), vs itself C; prudent: YES`\n\n| opponent Y   | X vs Y | Y vs X |\n|--------------|--------|--------|\n| CooperateBot | D      | C      |\n| DefectBot    | D      | D      |\n| FairBot      | C      | C      |\n| X itself     | C      | C      |\n\nTrace proof (worlds n = 0,1,2,…; □ψ at n means ψ at all m<n). Write ψ = a ∧ (d → □⊥); note □⊥ is true only at world 0.\n- vs CB: atoms a=c=d=⊤ always. ψ(m) = □⊥(m), true at m=0 only. So X = □ψ is C at n=0,1 and D for n≥2. Stable D.\n- vs DB: a=⊥ always, so ψ false at every m, X is C at 0 and D for n≥1. Stable D.\n- vs FB: FB's d-atom is \"FB vs DB\" = □⊥, true only at 0, where □⊥ is also true; so d→□⊥ holds at every world, and\n  ψ ≡ a = \"FB cooperates with X\" = □x. Induction: x_0 = f_0 = 1; if x_m = f_m = 1 for all m<n then f_n = 1 and x_n = 1.\n  Both C forever.\n- vs itself: d-atom = \"X vs DB\" = C only at world 0, where □⊥ is true, so d→□⊥ holds everywhere; ψ ≡ a = x, and\n  x_n = all x_m (m<n), which by induction is 1 forever. C.\nOther depth-2 prudent agents (all checked): `B(a) & B(~B(F) -> ~d)`, `B(a) & B(B(F) | ~d)`, `B(a) & (B(B(F)) | ~B(d))` (sol).\n\n## 2. No agent of modal depth < 2 is prudent (any size)\n\nDepth 0: a fully modalized formula of depth 0 contains no atoms, so it is a constant. ⊤ cooperates with CooperateBot;\n⊥ defects against FairBot. Neither is prudent.\n\nDepth 1: φ_X = g(□ψ_1, …, □ψ_k) for a Boolean function g and propositional formulas ψ_i in a, c, d (and constants).\nKey fact: the value of a fully modalized formula at world n depends only on the atom values at worlds m < n.\n\n(a) Against CooperateBot, the atoms (CB cooperates with X / with CB / with DB) are ⊤ at every world. So for n ≥ 1,\n□ψ_i(n) = ψ_i(1,1,1), independent of n; hence X's action vs CB is the same at every world n ≥ 1 and equals the stable\nvalue. Prudence requires it to be D: g(ψ_1(1,1,1), …, ψ_k(1,1,1)) = 0.\n\n(b) Against FairBot, at world 0 the opponent atoms are a = FB-vs-X(0) = □x(0) = ⊤, c = FB-vs-CB(0) = □⊤ = ⊤,\nd = FB-vs-DB(0) = □⊥(0) = ⊤ (all boxes are vacuously true at world 0). So at world 1, each □ψ_i(1) = ψ_i(1,1,1), and\nX's action vs FB at world 1 equals g(ψ_1(1,1,1), …) = 0 by (a): X defects against FB at world 1.\n\n(c) Then FairBot's action against X, □(X cooperates with FB), is false at every world n ≥ 2 (world 1 < n is a\ncounterexample), so FairBot's stable action against X is D, violating prudence.\n\nHence no agent of depth ≤ 1 is prudent, and the minimal depth is exactly 2. (Same argument found independently by sol.)\nMore generally the argument shows: any agent whose action vs CB is already stable at world 1 cannot be prudent; depth 2\nis needed so that X can see at world 2 the world-1 difference between FairBot (d false: FB defects vs DB) and\nCooperateBot (d true).\n\n## 3. Minimal size (partial / computational)\n\nCounting AST nodes (each atom, constant, ¬, ∧, ∨, →, □ counts 1), `opus/enum.py` enumerated all formulas by size up\nto 8, deduplicating subformulas semantically (by their value sequences on 202 test contexts — heuristic dedup, so this\nis strong evidence, not a proof). Results:\n- no prudent formula of size ≤ 6;\n- size 7: exactly one class, `B(a & (d -> B(F)))` (depth 2) — the answer above;\n- size 8: `B(a & (d -> B(~c)))`, `B(a & (d -> B(~d)))` (depth 2), and depth-3 variants `B(a & B(d -> B(F)))`,\n  `B(a & (d -> B(B(F))))`.\nStructural pattern of the minimal agents: □(a ∧ (d → θ)) with θ a □-formula (so θ is true at world 0 in every\ncontext). FairBot and X itself cooperate with DefectBot only at world 0, where θ is true, so the guard d → θ is\nharmless and the agent behaves like FairBot against them; CooperateBot cooperates with DB forever, so any θ that is\nfalse at some world m ≥ 1 against CB (□⊥, □¬c, □¬d, □□⊥ …) makes X defect against CB.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
